":"VeganRicha LLC"},"image":{"@id":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/#\/schema\/logo\/image\/"},"sameAs":["https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/VeganRicha","https:\/\/x.com\/veganricha","https:\/\/instagram.com\/veganricha\/","https:\/\/www.pinterest.com\/veganricha","https:\/\/youtube.com\/veganricharecipes"]},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/#\/schema\/person\/008994495d9faab5cd94cbec4069b445","name":"Richa","image":{"@type":"ImageObject","inLanguage":"en-US","@id":"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/517f2e68abf7632b27af8bafc9c52286649f86d9d1c25ee8936e2387fa8c2332?s=96&d=mm&r=g","url":"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/517f2e68abf7632b27af8bafc9c52286649f86d9d1c25ee8936e2387fa8c2332?s=96&d=mm&r=g","contentUrl":"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/517f2e68abf7632b27af8bafc9c52286649f86d9d1c25ee8936e2387fa8c2332?s=96&d=mm&r=g","caption":"Richa"},"description":"Hi, I'm Richa! I create flavorful plant based recipes that are inspired by my Indian upbringing, including many gluten-free, soy-free, and oil-free options.","sameAs":["https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/about-contact\/","https:\/\/x.com\/veganricha"],"url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/about-contact\/"},{"@type":"Recipe","name":"Vegan German Chocolate Cake Loaf","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Vegan Richa"},"description":"This Vegan German Chocolate Loaf Cake is a rich and moist chocolate cake baked in a loaf pan, with the traditional nutty pecan and coconut caramel filling running through the middle!","datePublished":"2021-04-07T03:46:31+00:00","image":["https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/German-Chocolate-Cake-4956.jpg","https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/German-Chocolate-Cake-4956-500x500.jpg","https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/German-Chocolate-Cake-4956-500x375.jpg","https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/03\/German-Chocolate-Cake-4956-480x270.jpg"],"video":{"name":"GERMAN CHOCOLATE LOAF CAKE | Vegan Richa Recipes","description":"GERMAN CHOCOLATE LOAF CAKE\n\n🔸Get the WRITTEN RECIPE here - https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/german-chocolate-loaf-cake\/\n\n🔸SUBSCRIBE HERE: https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/veganricharecipes?sub_confirmation=1\n\n🔸My New Instant pot cookbook: https:\/\/www.amazon.com\/Vegan-Richas-Instant-PotTM-Cookbook\/dp\/0306875039\/\n\nThis Vegan German Chocolate Loaf Cake is a rich and moist chocolate cake baked in a loaf pan, with the traditional nutty pecan and coconut caramel filling running through the middle!\n\nAnytime coconut is involved, any dessert has the potential to turn into one of my favorites!  I LOVE me a slice of classic German Chocolate Cake!  However, I hardly ever get around to making intricate layer cakes! This loaf cake version comes to the rescue! It is easier to put together—no layer cakes to fuss over—and it doesn’t lack one bit in the flavor department. Rich and chocolatey with the classic nutty caramel pecan filling, this easy vegan loaf cake is really hard to resist. I think you’ll love it!\n\n******MORE VEGAN DESSERT RECIPES FROM THE BLOG******\n\nVEGAN CARROT CAKE: https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/vegan-carrot-cake-recipe\/\n\nVEGAN COFFEE CAKE: https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/vegan-coffee-cake-recipe\/\n\nVEGAN LEMON BLUEBERRY CAKE: https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/lemon-blueberry-cake-yogurt-pound-cake-loaf\/\n\nCOOKBOOKS BY RICHA HINGLE (VEGAN RICHA): https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/mybooks\/\n\nConnect with me on Social Media:\n\nFACEBOOK: https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/VeganRicha\n\nINSTAGRAM: https:\/\/instagram.com\/veganricha\n\nPINTEREST: https:\/\/www.pinterest.com\/veganricha\/\n\nTWITTER: https:\/\/twitter.com\/veganricha\n\nMusic: Epidemic Sound \n\n#veganchocolatecake #loafcake #easyvegancake #easyveganrecipes","uploadDate":"2023-04-22T17:00:16+00:00","duration":"PT1M37S","thumbnailUrl":"https:\/\/i.ytimg.com\/vi\/Yrzx7l7h7jQ\/hqdefault.jpg","embedUrl":"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/embed\/Yrzx7l7h7jQ?feature=oembed","contentUrl":"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=Yrzx7l7h7jQ","@type":"VideoObject"},"recipeYield":["12"],"prepTime":"PT15M","cookTime":"PT55M","totalTime":"PT70M","recipeIngredient":["1 cup non dairy milk","1  shot of espresso (or use 1 tsp instant coffee mixed in two tbsp of hot water)","2 tsp vinegar (apple cider or white )","2 tbsp vegan yogurt or apple sauce","1\/4 cup oil","1\/3 cup sugar (use 2 tbsp more for sweeter)","1 tsp vanilla extract","1 1\/2 cups flour (I use all purpose)","1 tbsp corn starch","1\/3 cup cocoa powder","2 tsp baking powder","1\/4 tsp baking soda","1\/2 tsp salt","1 cup packed soft dates","1\/2 cup plus 2 tbsp non dairy milk","2 tbsp maple syrup","1\/3 cup toasted pecans","1 cup lightly toasted coconut","1\/4 tsp salt"],"recipeInstructions":[{"@type":"HowToSection","name":"To make the frosting:","itemListElement":[{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Soak the dates in hot water for at least 15 minutes, then drain. Blend the soaked dates with the milk, and maple syrup until well blended. If you haven&#039;t toasted the pecans and the coconut yet, add the pecans to a skillet over medium heat, and toast for 3-4 minutes, and add in the coconut and continue to toast for another 2-3 minutes.","name":"Soak the dates in hot water for at least 15 minutes, then drain. Blend the soaked dates with the milk, and maple syrup until well blended. If you haven&#039;t toasted the pecans and the coconut yet, add the pecans to a skillet over medium heat, and toast for 3-4 minutes, and add in the coconut and continue to toast for another 2-3 minutes.","url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/german-chocolate-loaf-cake\/#wprm-recipe-34889-step-0-0"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Mix this pecan coconut mixture into the blended date mixture. Add in the salt. Mix well. This is your frosting that you will layer on the cake.","name":"Mix this pecan coconut mixture into the blended date mixture. Add in the salt. Mix well. This is your frosting that you will layer on the cake.","url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/german-chocolate-loaf-cake\/#wprm-recipe-34889-step-0-1"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Mix all the dry ingredients for the cake in a bowl, until well combined.","name":"Mix all the dry ingredients for the cake in a bowl, until well combined.","url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/german-chocolate-loaf-cake\/#wprm-recipe-34889-step-0-2"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Heat the milk until it is hot, then add to a bowl. add in all of the rest of the wet ingredients and mix well. Add the dry to the wet ingredients, and mix well until you get a somewhat thick batter. If the batter is too thick, add in a tbsp or more of nondairy milk.","name":"Heat the milk until it is hot, then add to a bowl. add in all of the rest of the wet ingredients and mix well. Add the dry to the wet ingredients, and mix well until you get a somewhat thick batter. If the batter is too thick, add in a tbsp or more of nondairy milk.","url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/german-chocolate-loaf-cake\/#wprm-recipe-34889-step-0-3"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Add half of the batter to a lined 9x5 inch loaf pan, even it out, then top it with half of the frosting mixture. Add in the rest of the batter, then top it with the rest of the frosting mixture.","name":"Add half of the batter to a lined 9x5 inch loaf pan, even it out, then top it with half of the frosting mixture. Add in the rest of the batter, then top it with the rest of the frosting mixture.","url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/german-chocolate-loaf-cake\/#wprm-recipe-34889-step-0-4"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Bake at 375 degrees F (190 c ) for 45 - 55 minutes. Cover the pan lightly with parchment after the first 35 minutes so that the top frosting doesn&#039;t get too crusty or burnt.","name":"Bake at 375 degrees F (190 c ) for 45 - 55 minutes. Cover the pan lightly with parchment after the first 35 minutes so that the top frosting doesn&#039;t get too crusty or burnt.","url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/german-chocolate-loaf-cake\/#wprm-recipe-34889-step-0-5"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Check the toothpick from the center of the loaf to see if its done. (Check at 45 mins as ovens and pans vary, the toothpick shouldn’t have any chocolate batter )","name":"Check the toothpick from the center of the loaf to see if its done. (Check at 45 mins as ovens and pans vary, the toothpick shouldn’t have any chocolate batter )","url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/german-chocolate-loaf-cake\/#wprm-recipe-34889-step-0-6"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Once the cake has been sitting in the pan for 15 minutes, take it out of the pan. You can additionally add a drizzle of melted chocolate on top for a better look, and chocolate flavor.","name":"Once the cake has been sitting in the pan for 15 minutes, take it out of the pan. You can additionally add a drizzle of melted chocolate on top for a better look, and chocolate flavor.","url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/german-chocolate-loaf-cake\/#wprm-recipe-34889-step-0-7"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Cool completely before slicing. Store on the counter for up to a day, and in the fridge for up to 7 days.","name":"Cool completely before slicing. Store on the counter for up to a day, and in the fridge for up to 7 days.","url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/german-chocolate-loaf-cake\/#wprm-recipe-34889-step-0-8"}]}],"aggregateRating":{"@type":"AggregateRating","ratingValue":"5","ratingCount":"14","reviewCount":"3"},"review":[{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"Really great recipe","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Annette"},"datePublished":"2021-11-01"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"Very nice recipe","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"AmbalaCakes"},"datePublished":"2021-10-29"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"Sooo good! Everyone loved this cake for Mother’s Day. I want to try the muffin version next!","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Cheryl Cross"},"datePublished":"2021-05-09"}],"recipeCategory":["Breakfast","brunch","Dessert"],"recipeCuisine":["American"],"keywords":"German Chocolate loaf cake, Vegan chocolate loaf cake","nutrition":{"@type":"NutritionInformation","calories":"247 kcal","carbohydrateContent":"34 g","proteinContent":"4 g","fatContent":"12 g","saturatedFatContent":"5 g","sodiumContent":"205 mg","fiberContent":"4 g","sugarContent":"17 g","servingSize":"1 serving"},"@id":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/german-chocolate-loaf-cake\/#recipe","isPartOf":{"@id":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/german-chocolate-loaf-cake\/#article"},"mainEntityOfPage":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/german-chocolate-loaf-cake\/"}]}</script>
